Third-party text quoted for reproducibility
-------------------------------------------

The files below hold sentences rewritten by Grammarly's hosted service, or
example sentences published in Grammarly's own documentation, harvested on
2026-08-29 and 2026-08-30. They exist so that the published comparison numbers
can be re-derived by a reader, and they are quoted for that purpose. They are
NOT the author's work, are NOT licensed by the author to anyone, and are
covered by neither LICENSE nor LICENSE-DATA:

  bench/corpus/grammarly-pairs.json               200 sentences typed into
      Grammarly's editor with every suggestion accepted; 118 of the 200 came
      back changed. The 118 rewrites are Grammarly's output. Four instruments
      read this file; bench/corpus/THIRD-PARTY.md says which and why.
  bench/corpus/oracle-labels.json                 author-written meaning labels
      that quote the Grammarly rewrite each one judges, in its `grammarly`
      field. The labelling is the author's; the quoted rewrite is not.
  bench/corpus/grammarly-dev.json                 66 rows: 54 whose source
      sentences come from Grammarly's published documentation, and a 12-row
      comparison battery.

Two further collections were removed from the tree on 2026-09-02 because no
instrument read them: grammarly-reference.json (every suggestion card
transcribed, with Grammarly's own category labels) and
grammarly-correctness-pairs.json. They remain in git history until that
history is rewritten before the repository is made public.

